{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs1nf9VqZHtQrPnKstwF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A constrained package is now exempt from the `--max-release-age` filter, so a pin like `boto3==1.35.88` no longer disappears from resolution. The regression test passes, and `tests/test_cooldown.py` plus `tests/test_resolver.py` pass (70 tests).\n\n**Change** (`src/fromager/resolver.py`, `find_all_matching_from_provider`)\n- If the provider's constraints contain the requirement, the age cutoff is set to `None` and an info log says so. The old \"keeping all to avoid empty resolution\" warning no longer fires for pinned packages.\n- I put the check here because every caller (bootstrap resolver, `sources.py`, the cache fallback) goes through this function.\n- I also documented the behavior in the `max_age_cutoff` docstring.\n\n**Test** (`tests/test_cooldown.py`, `test_max_release_age_skipped_for_constrained_package`)\n- Constraint `test-pkg==1.2.2`, cutoff set so every candidate is too old, and `fallback_on_empty_age_filter=False` (multi-version mode). The old code returns `[]`; the new code returns the pinned `1.2.2`.\n- I reasoned through the old behavior rather than running the test against the unfixed code.\n\n**Decisions you may want to review**\n- I treated any constraint as explicit intent, not just `==` pins. The ticket's wording (\"a constraint is explicit user intent\") points this way. If you want only exact pins to bypass the age filter, the check needs to look at the specifier.\n- The existing `resolve_package_cooldown` already exempts top-level `==` pins from the cooldown. I did not change that code.\n\n**Not run:** `ruff` and `mypy` are not in `.venv`, so I did not run lint or type checks. The project's `hatch run lint:fix` / `mypy:check` should be run before committing. I did not commit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,